(Autonomous Edge Computing: Architecture, Protocols, and Resilience) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -18 Td
(Department of Computer Science & Engineering - Technical Research Report) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(ABSTRACT) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -18 Td
(Edge computing addresses latency and bandwidth limitations by executing data processing) Tj
0 -18 Td
(closer to edge sensors rather than depending exclusively on centralized cloud data centers.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(In this study, we present an autonomous edge computing architecture tailored for high-frequency) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Internet of Things \(IoT\) workloads. Our approach introduces localized state arbitration, zero-loss) Tj
0 -18 Td
(fault recovery, and lightweight telemetry caching. Benchmarks across 50 simulated edge clusters) Tj
0 -18 Td
(demonstrate a 68 percent reduction in packet transmission latency and a 42 percent savings in) Tj
0 -18 Td
(backhaul network bandwidth compared to traditional cloud-only ingestion models.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(1. INTRODUCTION AND MOTIVATION) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -18 Td
(The exponential proliferation of smart infrastructure, autonomous vehicles, and industrial sensors) Tj
0 -18 Td
(has overwhelmed conventional cloud storage pipelines. Transmitting raw telemetry across wide-area) Tj
0 -18 Td
(networks introduces unpredictable network jitter, high transit costs, and vulnerabilities to intermittent) Tj
0 -18 Td
(connectivity failures. Edge computing bridges this gap by provisioning decentralized micro-clusters.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(By filtering and aggregating telemetry at the ingress gateway, edge systems insulate critical control loops) Tj
0 -18 Td
(from wide-area communication drops. However, deploying computation to untrusted, resource-constrained) Tj
0 -18 Td
(nodes introduces formidable challenges in decentralized data synchronization and fault tolerance.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(This project outlines an algorithmic framework for edge self-orchestration that enables edge clusters) Tj
0 -18 Td
(to sustain localized processing even during extended wide-area network partitions.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 1725 >>
stream
BT
/F1 14 Tf
50 740 Td
(2. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE AND CORE MODULES) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -18 Td
(The proposed system consists of three hierarchical layers: Sensing, Edge Gateway, and Cloud Core.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(A. Sensor Ingestion Layer) Tj
0 -18 Td
(IoT field devices interface with local micro-gateways using lightweight telemetry protocols such as MQTT) Tj
0 -18 Td
(and CoAP. Ingestion buffers utilize ring-buffer queues to prevent memory overflow during telemetry spikes.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(B. Edge Processing Gateway \(Fog Layer\)) Tj
0 -18 Td
(The gateway layer hosts lightweight containers responsible for real-time anomaly detection, local rule) Tj
0 -18 Td
(enforcement, and sliding-window statistical aggregation. A local storage engine maintains time-series) Tj
0 -18 Td
(snapshots to handle transient network disconnects without data degradation.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(C. Centralized Cloud Coordination Core) Tj
0 -18 Td
(The cloud layer acts as a global coordinator. It aggregates summarized metrics from distributed edge clusters,) Tj
0 -18 Td
(coordinates global policy updates, and conducts deep historical auditing using scalable data lakes.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(3. RETRIEVAL AND REPLICATION PROTOCOLS) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -18 Td
(Our framework implements an epoch-based gossip replication protocol. Edge nodes maintain vector clocks) Tj
0 -18 Td
(to track causality between concurrent data events. When a network partition is healed, nodes reconcile) Tj
0 -18 Td
(conflicting updates using deterministic CRDT \(Conflict-Free Replicated Data Type\) state merging.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(This ensures eventual consistency without requiring centralized global locking overhead.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
