stream
BT
/F1 14 Tf
50 740 Td
(4. EXPERIMENTAL EVALUATION AND RESULTS) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -18 Td
(To evaluate our architecture, we conducted rigorous benchmarks across a distributed testbed of 50 virtualized) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Raspberry Pi nodes connected to a central server with simulated WAN latency variations \(10ms to 250ms\).) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Latency Reduction: End-to-end response times dropped from 240ms in cloud models to 28ms under local edge processing.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Network Bandwidth Savings: Ingress bandwidth consumption fell by 42.4 percent due to localized feature aggregation.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Fault Tolerance: Nodes demonstrated uninterrupted operation during a simulated 45-minute cloud link partition.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Recovery Time: Upon reconnection, full vector state synchronization completed in under 1.8 seconds.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(5. CONCLUSION AND FUTURE SCOPE) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -18 Td
(This research validates that decentralized edge architectures significantly outperform traditional centralized) Tj
0 -18 Td
(architectures in latency-sensitive industrial applications. Local telemetry processing protects real-time control) Tj
0 -18 Td
(loops while drastically curbing cloud transit overhead.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(Future enhancements will investigate lightweight machine learning inference at the edge using quantization,) Tj
0 -18 Td
(energy-aware dynamic load balancing, and zero-knowledge cryptographic verification for edge-to-cloud streams.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 11 Tf
